e n-k\\)*, then \\((a,b)\\) lies on the horizontal line \\(H_b\\).\n\n   *If \\(b\\ge n-k+1\\)*, set \\(d=b-a\\).  \n   From \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) we obtain  \n\n   \\[\n   d=b-a\\le (n+1-a)-a=n+1-2a\\le n-1,\n   \\]\n   because \\(a\\ge1\\).  \n   Moreover \\(b\\ge n-k+1\\) gives  \n\n   \\[\n   d=b-a\\ge n-k+1-a\\ge n-k,\n   \\]\n   since \\(a\\le k\\) (otherwise \\(a+b>k+(n-k+1)=n+1\\), contradicting \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\)).  \n   Hence \\(d\\in\\{n-k,\\dots ,n-1\\}\\) and \\((a,b)\\) satisfies \\(b=a+d\\), i.e. it lies on the sunny line \\(S_d\\).\n\n   Thus every point of \\(T_n\\) belongs to at least one of the \\(n\\) constructed lines, and exactly \\(k\\) of them (the \\(S_d\\)’s) are sunny.\n\n4. **Conclusion.**  \n   The construction works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\); the necessary condition \\(k\\le n\\) is also sufficient. Hence the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,0\\le k\\le n\\, } .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
